    "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\r\nPLEASE FILL IN THE PR DESCRIPTION HERE ENSURING ALL CHECKLIST ITEMS (AT THE BOTTOM) HAVE BEEN CONSIDERED.\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nOn SM90+ (Hopper / L20X), load fused MoE expert weights `B` with `tl.make_tensor_descriptor` so Triton can emit real **TMA** for `(BN, BK)` tiles. `B` is `(E, N, K)` with K contiguous; each expert is described as `(N, K)`, expert selected by base pointer offset. Pre-SM90 keeps the original pointer `tl.load` path. With `SWAP_AB`, use the TMA tile as-is; otherwise `tl.trans` before `tl.dot`.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n- [x] Kernel microbench: `benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_moe.py --model mistralai/Mixtral-8x7B-Instruct-v0.1 --tp-size 2` (default batch list), compare parent commit vs this change on SM90+\r\n- [x] ncu analyze on `fused_moe_kernel` for a large-M shape\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n### benchmark\r\n**Env:** L20X ×4 (SM 9.0), Mixtral-8x7B, tp=2, no EP, default configs.  \r\n**Baseline:** `615834ee5` · **This PR:** `67079d25d` (descriptor TMA). Metric: Kernel time (µs).\r\n\r\n| batch | before | after | speedup |\r\n|------:|-------:|------:|--------:|\r\n| 1 | 107.01 | 109.41 | 0.978x |\r\n| 2 | 166.39 | 166.45 | 1.000x |\r\n| 4 | 255.53 | 255.24 | 1.001x |\r\n| 8 | 321.42 | 323.10 | 0.995x |\r\n| 16 | 347.74 | 348.08 | 0.999x |\r\n| 24 | 352.14 | 352.99 | 0.998x |\r\n| 32 | 354.04 | 353.19 | 1.002x |\r\n| 48 | 358.34 | 356.82 | 1.004x |\r\n| 64 | 361.24 | 359.87 | 1.004x |\r\n| 96 | 378.70 | 373.26 | 1.015x |\r\n| 128 | 383.61 | 375.21 | 1.022x |\r\n| 256 | 484.41 | 477.96 | 1.013x |\r\n| 512 | 799.75 | 781.34 | 1.024x |\r\n| 1024 | 1098.69 | 1029.15 | 1.068x |\r\n| 1536 | 1430.04 | 1345.79 | 1.063x |\r\n| 2048 | 1827.13 | 1714.26 | 1.066x |\r\n| 3072 | 2615.87 | 2449.06 | 1.068x |\r\n| 4096 | 3401.02 | 3172.54 | 1.072x |\r\n\r\nSmall M ≈ flat; large M (~1024+) about **6–7%** faster. Kernel microbench only; not e2e.\r\n\r\n### NCU profiling\r\n| Item | Value |\r\n|------|--------|\r\n| Model | `tencent/HunyuanImage-3.0-Instruct` |\r\n| GPU | NVIDIA L20X (SM 9.0) |\r\n| MoE shape (TP4 EP) | local E=16, topk=8, hidden=4096, w2 intermediate=3072 |\r\n| Replay | `--shape M=8194`, `--self-builder vllm_triton_experts:...`, `--int-max 16 --warmup 1` |\r\n\r\n**before**:\r\n<img width=\"2330\" height=\"410\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8752fc5f-ee4c-4dbc-9858-4a06cb787b4a\" />\r\n\r\n**after**:\r\n<img width=\"1960\" height=\"396\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b21d996b-3546-43c2-8e7e-5176c346b23b\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>** (anything written below this line will be removed by GitHub Actions)\r\n",
